{
  "name": "Weekly hiring signals for recruiters: LinkedIn jobs grouped by company to Slack and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Weekly hiring signals for recruiters: LinkedIn jobs → companies hiring → Slack + Google Sheets\n\nCompanies that post several jobs for the same kind of role this week are your warmest leads. Every Monday morning this workflow searches LinkedIn job posts for your roles and location, groups them **by company**, and posts a short digest to Slack: who is hiring, how many open roles, which titles, company size and industry. Every company also gets a row in a Google Sheet, so you can see who keeps hiring week after week.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Apify `santamaria-automations/linkedin-scraper` (no LinkedIn login) returns the job posts from the last 7 days for each search in **Settings**.\n2. A Code node groups the posts by company, drops staffing and recruitment agencies (your competitors, not your clients; detected from industry, name and LinkedIn description) and any company on your exclude list, and keeps companies with at least `minOpenRoles` posts.\n3. The companies are written to the **Hiring signals** tab (one row per company per week; a second run in the same week updates those rows) and the top companies go to Slack in one message.\n\n**Setup (about 10 minutes)**\n1. Install the verified community node `@apify/n8n-nodes-apify` (tested with 0.9.0; install guide: https://docs.apify.com/platform/integrations/n8n). It works on n8n Cloud and self-hosted. Connect your Apify account in **Search LinkedIn jobs** (OAuth2 on Cloud, or an API token).\n2. Connect Google Sheets (Sheet and HTTP nodes). On the first run the workflow creates the Sheet **Hiring signals - NanoScrape** in your Drive with a **Hiring signals** tab and header row; later runs find it by name.\n3. Open **Settings**: your searches (one role per line), location, minimum open roles, companies to exclude and Slack channel name.\n4. Connect Slack (the bot must be invited to the channel).\n5. Test with **Test workflow**, then activate. The trigger runs Mondays at 8 AM (your n8n timezone).\n\n**Times:** the week label and the Monday schedule use your n8n timezone (Settings → Timezone).\n\n**Tested on** n8n 2.35.7 and 2.47.7 (self-hosted), 2026-11-16.\n\n**Cost** (Apify Store prices, checked 2026-11-16): $0.001 per job post plus $0.001 per run. 3 searches × 100 posts ≈ $0.30 a week. **Max cost per run** in the Apify node caps every run.\n\n**Limits**\n- Only public LinkedIn job posts are used; no logins and no personal profiles. Company size and industry come from the company's LinkedIn page and can be missing.\n- The agency filter is a keyword check; in our London test (38 companies) it caught 9 of 11 agencies and dropped no employer. Add the rest to `excludeCompanies` once and they stay out.\n- The same company can appear under slightly different names on different posts.\n- Communities, networks and job boards that post partner jobs (not recruitment agencies) can show up as companies. Add them to `excludeCompanies`.",
        "height": 1160,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
